inherits it either: the published type definitions and schemas are vocabulary,
not code. The validator and the fixtures beside them in schema/ are code, and
are Apache-2.0. Both directories carried their own licence file from the first
commit that created them.


SPDX HEADERS
============

Every source file carries an SPDX-License-Identifier header, so that a single
file stays self-describing once it leaves this tree:

  TypeScript, JavaScript   // SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
  Markdown                 an SPDX line in the document
  JSON                     "$comment": "SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0"
                           -- JSON has no comment syntax, so SPDX rides in a
                           field

Where a file is vocabulary rather than code, its SPDX identifier is CC-BY-4.0
or CC-BY-SA-4.0 accordingly, and the identifier in the file wins over any
inference from its directory.


